    <h1>🔬 The Formatter's Lab</h1>
    <p>Welcome to the lab where we style text like scientists style experiments — with precision and purpose! Each section shows a different formatting tag in action and their uses.</p>

    <h2>Bold vs Strong</h2>
    <p>The <b>cheetah</b> is the fastest land animal on Earth and is known for its incredible speed.</p>
    <p>You should <strong>always wear a helmet</strong> when riding a bicycle and never ride without one.</p>

    <h2>Italic vs Emphasis</h2>
    <p>The scientific name for a lion is <i>Panthera leo</i>.</p>
    <p>This is <em>really</em> important — never touch an unknown chemical without protective gloves and eyewear.</p>

    <h2>Highlight and Small</h2>
    <p>Remember: <mark>water boils at 100°C</mark> at sea level and is essential for life.</p>
    <p>The Sun is about 150 million km away from Earth and provides energy for all life on the planet. <small>(approximately)</small></p>

    <h2>Deleted text</h2>
    <p>Pluto is a <del>planet</del> dwarf planet and not a full planet.</p>
    <p>The Great Wall of China is <del>visible from space</del>. This is actually a myth and not true as it is not visible from space.</p>

    <h2>Superscript and Subscript</h2>
    <p>The area of a circle is πr<sup>2</sup>.</p>
    <p>Water is made of H<sub>2</sub>O — two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom but not a simple molecule.</p>
    <p>Einstein's most famous equation is E = mc<sup>2</sup> even though it's not a simple equation.</p>

  </body>
</html>